      "edits": [
        {
          "modify_from": "At later act cycles, inspect the current pose and the motion frames for arrival at pattern[incoming reached_index + 1]. If the stick has reached that node within 1 cm and the visible endpoint activation supports arrival, increment by one; otherwise retain the incoming value. Never increment merely because you are about to command a move. If no steps executed, retain the value.",
          "modify_to": "At later act cycles, start a working index at incoming reached_index and scan the motion frames chronologically, using the current wrist image and TCP pose as additional evidence. Whenever arrival at pattern[working index + 1] is established by stick position within 1 cm and supporting endpoint activation, increment the working index and continue checking for arrival at its successor. Confirm every consecutive arrival shown, without a one-increment-per-cycle limit. Write the final working index. Proximity outside 1 cm, an action-only near-arrival allowance, or choosing an onward waypoint does not advance this field. If no steps executed, retain the incoming value."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "policy_prompt_for_action": [
    {
      "modify_from": "Determine the latest reached index using the incoming reached_index and observed arrival at its next node, applying the memory update rule. If another node remains, command exactly that next node's world x and y, z=0.070 m, retaining the current approximately downward TCP orientation.",
      "modify_to": "Compute the latest strictly confirmed index by applying the memory update rule to all this cycle's motion frames, confirming every consecutive arrival shown without a one-arrival limit. Normally select the node immediately after that index. If steps have executed, the current TCP is within 0.012 m of that node's ideal waypoint, and the observed motion is consistent with finishing the segment to it, treat that one node as complete for action selection and select its successor instead. This allowance does not change reached_index, does not apply recursively, and cannot skip any other unconfirmed node. If a target remains, command exactly its ideal world x and y, z=0.070 m, retaining the current approximately downward TCP orientation."
    },
    {
      "modify_from": "Arrival within 1 cm is sufficient to move on; do not unnecessarily correct the few-millimetre residual errors shown after motions.",
      "modify_to": "Strictly confirmed arrival or the action-only near-arrival case above is sufficient to move on; do not correct residual errors covered by these conditions."
    },
    {
      "modify_from": "If the next endpoint has not been reached, target that same endpoint rather than skipping it.",
      "modify_to": "Retry the next unconfirmed endpoint only when neither strict confirmation nor the action-only near-arrival case applies."
    },
    {
      "modify_from": "Once the final endpoint is visibly reached, make no additional tracing motion; if another response is required before automatic termination, wait a single control step to allow success evaluation.",
      "modify_to": "Once the final endpoint is strictly confirmed or satisfies the action-only near-arrival case, make no additional tracing motion; if another response is required before automatic termination, wait a single control step to allow success evaluation."
